**Read:** [Common Waste Water and Waste Gas Treatment/Management Systems in the Chemical Sector, BREF CWW](../sources/Chemical-Sector-Water-and-Waste-BREF.lingua#r_3DD06XBCANC091G38HBZ4BX7Y9), the entire wastewater inventory, collection, characterization, treatment, sludge and return-water treatment; [Biochemical conversion of corn stover to ethanol — Humbird and colleagues](../sources/Biochemical-Ethanol-Design-Humbird.lingua#r_123G817BYJFAVYGA0ZVK3J5FJH), the complete wastewater and utility design/account sections; [Manufacture of Organic Fine Chemicals, BREF OFC](../sources/Organic-Fine-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_0DH473049K4WX7HAAY1P7SDS3K), the full relevant process-integrated water and residual case.

Wastewater is a changing chemical mixture whose treatment depends on speciation, concentrations, phases, temperature, variability and intended destination. A total or surrogate measure such as organic load cannot identify every toxic, reactive, persistent or recoverable constituent. Sampling and analytical support define the quantity being inferred.

Prevention, segregation, equalization, recovery, physical separation, chemical reaction and biological treatment perform different tasks. Removing a species from water can transfer it to air, sludge, a concentrated regenerant or recovered product. An apparently cleaner liquid therefore needs a complete constituent and residual account.

Trace water quality and return to process. Recycling can reduce fresh demand while concentrating salts or other contaminants and changing equipment/product behavior. Compare actual loads and useful-quality requirements rather than simply counting a reused water volume as equivalent to fresh supply.

**Work:** reconstruct the complete wastewater inventory and treatment/recovery train for one chemical route. Independently close water and at least two consequential constituents across all phases, with uncertainty and changing inventories. Compare a documented prevention/recovery alternative and identify the primary observation needed to test its effect on product, utilities and residuals elsewhere in the system.

**Continue:** [Explain air releases through source chemistry, transport, measurement and actual treatment](Gases-vapors-diffuse-losses-capture-and-chemical-fate.lingua#r_7KTHFESRPTNWH9ZXEV12K27JW0).

